==English==
[[File:Flower trellis 1.jpg|thumb|A trellis for growing climbing plants]]
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|trelis|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|treleis||lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|treille||lang=fro|arbor}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|trichila||lang=la|arbor", "summer house}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtrɛlɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|trellises}}

# An outdoor garden [[frame]] which can be used for partitioning a common area.
# An outdoor garden frame which can be used to grow vines or other climbing plants.
# {{context|computing theory}} A kind of [[graph]] used in [[communication theory]] and [[encryption]].

